--TEST--
Core\Math::abs refuses a `string` where the call is written, with the mismatch a parameter declared `int|float|decimal` reports, even though its result follows the argument's type, per spec § 3
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The variable `abs` binds from its argument has a bound. A `string` does not
// fit it, so the parameter reads as the bound and the call does not compile.
echo Core\Math::abs("-3"), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `int|float|decimal`, found `string`
  --> case.nvs:4:21
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
